    "message": {
     "content": "### The Verdict\n\n**Yes, you should strongly lean toward taking this offer.** \n\nThis is a massive turnaround from the initial package. By securing a **$200,000 cash sign-on bonus**, Google has effectively bought out your entire unvested Meta equity in guaranteed cash upfront, while still giving you the full $1.08M equity grant on top of it.\n\n---\n\n### The New Financial Reality\n\n| Component | Meta (IC6) | Google Revised Offer (L6) | Delta |\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\n| **Base Salary** | $240,000 | $240,000 | $0 (Parity reached) |\n| **Target Bonus** | $36,000 | $48,000 | +$12,000 |\n| **RSUs (Annual Run-Rate)** | ~$250,000 | $270,000* | +$20,000 |\n| **Sign-On Bonus** | $0 | **$200,000** | **+$200,000 (Cash)** |\n| **Year 1 Total Comp** | **~$526,000** | **~$758,000** | **+$232,000 (+44%)** |\n\n*\\*Note on Google Equity Vesting:* Google frequently uses a front-loaded vesting schedule (e.g., 33% Year 1, 33% Year 2, 22% Year 3, 12% Year 4). If your offer uses this schedule, your Year 1 equity vesting will actually be **~$356,400**, pushing your **Year 1 Total Compensation to ~$844,000**.\n\n---\n\n### Why This Is an Exceptional Outcome\n\n1. **Guaranteed Liquid Upside:** An extra $200,000 in cash in Year 1 eliminates the transition risk. Even if you stayed at Meta, that $200,000 was tied up in future vesting schedules and stock price fluctuations.\n2. **Top-of-Band Sign-On for L6:** A $200k sign-on bonus for an L6 PM is at the very top percentile for Google. They clearly stretched to close this gap.\n3. **Multi-Year Comp Stability:** In Years 2\u20134, your baseline comp (excluding refreshes) sits around **$558,000/yr**. As refreshers stack, you will comfortably clear $600k\u2013$700k+ annually.\n\n---\n\n### 3 Things to Verify Before Signing\n\nBefore you put pen to paper, ask the recruiter to clarify these specific operational details in the written contract:\n\n1. **Sign-On Disbursement & Clawback Terms:**\n   * *Payment Timing:* Is it paid in one lump sum within your first 30\u201360 days, or split across Year 1 and Year 2 (e.g., $100k Y1 / $100k Y2)?\n   * *Clawback:* Ensure the clawback is prorated (e.g., if you leave after 11 months, you only repay 1/12th, rather than 100%).\n2. **Equity Vesting Schedule:**\n   * Confirm whether the $1.08M vests evenly (25% per year) or on Google\u2019s front-loaded schedule (33% / 33% / 22% / 12%).\n3. **Team & Scope Fit:**\n   * At Meta, IC6 PMs typically enjoy wide autonomy and fast execution cycles. At Google, L6 is a senior terminal level where consensus building and cross-functional alignment dominate. Ensure you are excited about your specific product area, manager, and team charter.\n\n---\n\n### Conclusion\n\nIf the team and scope look solid, **accept the offer**. You successfully negotiated a **44%+ Year 1 pay bump ($758k+ total comp)** without taking a hit to your base salary.",
